course: dictionary
lesson: 1439
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word stays the same, but the clues around it change. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: «Many UK shops charge for carrier bags so people use fewer.» Here a carrier is a bag for shopping, because the sentence is about bags that shops charge for. In «The cat carrier was empty», a carrier is a box for carrying a pet. Same word, different meaning, and the clues tell you which.
explain: Some meanings are about people or companies. «The mail carrier brought the letter» means a person who delivers post. «Her phone carrier raised its prices» means a company that gives mobile phone service. Check the clues before you choose.
fact: Carrier means a person, animal, vehicle or company that carries or delivers things or people.
fact: Carrier can also mean a bag, box or holder for carrying something, such as a carrier bag or a pet carrier.
fact: A carrier of a disease has germs and can pass them to others, sometimes without being ill.
fact: Mosquitoes are carriers of diseases like malaria, and washing your hands stops germs spreading.
fact: An aircraft carrier is a huge ship that planes take off from.
exercise: «Many UK shops charge for carrier bags.» What is a carrier in this sentence? | An animal that spreads germs | A person who delivers letters | *A bag for carrying shopping | A ship that planes take off from
exercise: «The cat carrier was on the floor at the vet's.» What is a carrier here? | A bag for shopping | A company that gives phone service | *A box for carrying a pet | A person who delivers post
exercise: Mosquitoes can be carriers of malaria. What does carrier mean here? | A company that flies planes | A pest that is never a problem | A holder for carrying shopping | *An animal that can pass germs to others
test: Which phrase means a huge ship that planes take off from? | pet carrier | carrier bag | *aircraft carrier | mail carrier
test: Which sentence uses carrier to mean a company? | *«Her phone carrier raised its prices.» | «She bought a bag at the shop.» | «The carrier bag was heavy.» | «The pet carrier was empty.»
exam: Look at «The mail carrier brought a parcel to our door.» What does carrier mean here? | A ship for planes | A bag for shopping | A germ that spreads disease | *A person who delivers post
